{title: Take My Life and Let It Be}
{artist: Frances R. Havergal / Henri Malan}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{key_original: F}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}
{score: take-my-life-and-let-it-be.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Take my life, and let it [C]be
[G]Consecrated, [D]Lord, to [G]Thee
[G]Take my moments and my [C]days
[G]Let them flow in [D]ceaseless [G]praise
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Take my hands, and let them [C]move
[G]At the impulse [D]of Thy [G]love
[G]Take my feet, and let them [C]be
[G]Swift and beauti[D]ful for [G]Thee
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Take my voice, and let me [C]sing
[G]Always, only, [D]for my [G]King
[G]Take my lips, and let them [C]be
[G]Filled with messa[D]ges from [G]Thee
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Take my silver and my [C]gold
[G]Not a mite would [D]I with[G]hold
[G]Take my intellect, and [C]use
[G]Every power as [D]Thou shalt [G]choose
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]Take my will, and make it [C]Thine
[G]It shall be no [D]longer [G]mine
[G]Take my heart, it is Thine [C]own
[G]It shall be Thy [D]royal [G]throne
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[G]Take my love, my Lord, I [C]pour
[G]At Thy feet its [D]treasure [G]store
[G]Take myself, and I will [C]be
[G]Ever, only, [D]all for [G]Thee
{end_of_verse}
